---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How is Kery different from plain Playwright?',
    a: 'Playwright executes scripts you write. Kery explores your app autonomously, finds bugs, and compiles the run into a Playwright script. You get test coverage without writing selectors or page objects.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is Kery different from Playwright codegen?',
    a: 'Codegen records your manual clicks. Kery explores on its own - it opens a real browser, navigates your app, identifies flows, and reports bugs without you touching a mouse.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does a typical run cost?',
    a: 'First exploratory run: ~$0.02–$0.05 depending on app complexity and model choice. Each regression replay after that: ~$0.001. Cost drops roughly 95% once a run compiles to a script.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need an LLM API key?',
    a: 'Yes, for exploratory runs. You bring your own key - OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or OpenRouter. Regression replays run as deterministic Playwright with no model calls.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens when a regression test fails?',
    a: 'The heal agent fires on the specific failing step. It reads the accessibility tree, identifies the broken selector, patches it in one shot, and hands control back to the replay. The output is a corrected .spec.ts file.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it work behind authentication?',
    a: 'Yes. Clerk, Supabase Auth, OAuth 2.0, GitHub, API tokens, and TOTP/2FA are all supported natively. Kery authenticates as part of the run - auth pages are not a wall.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I run Kery in CI?',
    a: 'Yes. Compiled regression scripts are standard Playwright .spec.ts files that run in any CI environment. The Kery server can also be triggered via API or MCP.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What can I do with MCP?',
    a: 'Trigger runs, pull bug reports, and inspect run history directly from Claude, Cursor, Copilot, or Codex without leaving your editor.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my data live?',
    a: 'In your own Postgres on your own infrastructure. Nothing leaves your environment.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What license applies?',
    a: 'Apache 2.0.',
  },
];
import HangingMango from './HangingMango.astro';
---

<hr class="section-divider" />
<section class="faq-section section">
  <HangingMango left="18%" wire={58} delay={0.6} />
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <span class="section-badge">FAQ</span>
      <h2>Short answers.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list reveal">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-question">{faq.q}</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{faq.a}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-section {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .faq-section h2 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .faq-list {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .faq-question {
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1rem;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-question::after {
    content: '+';
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-question::after {
    content: '−';
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
</style>
